24d8|n|The act or result of turning over; an upset; as, a bad turnover in a carriage. ; A semicircular pie or tart made by turning one half of a circular crust over the other, inclosing the fruit or other materials. ; An apprentice, in any trade, who is handed over from one master to another to complete his time.	a:xvm,40,2~xvm,40,2	n:1xc2,67,3;qul,58,6~qul,58,6;1xc2,67,3
